mt6789_balance — balanced CPU frequency policy for MT6789 (boot boost, touch floor,
screen-off cap), ported from itel-rs4-kernel patches/rs4/rs4_balance.c (same SoC).
Changes vs the RS4: touch floor is a direct freq_qos request (no Samsung cpufreq_limit);
the screen-off cap arms only after lcd-backlight has been seen lit, so a ROM whose
brightness bypasses the LED class (stale 0) can never leave the phone capped in use.
Default numbers are the RS4's, unvalidated on this phone; all are runtime tunables in
/sys/module/mt6789_balance/parameters/.
KMI      : new built-in driver on core APIs only; no struct or signature change.

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig b/drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig
index a18c22878..e01ee1516 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig
@@ -234,6 +234,17 @@ config CPU_FREQ_GOV_REFLEX
 
 	  If in doubt, say M.
 
+config MT6789_BALANCE
+	bool "MT6789 balanced CPU frequency policy"
+	depends on CPU_FREQ && INPUT && LEDS_CLASS
+	help
+	  Boot boost, a modest touch floor and a screen-off cap for MT6789
+	  phones (6x Cortex-A55 policy0 + 2x Cortex-A76 policy6), all as
+	  freq_qos requests on top of whatever governor runs. Tunables in
+	  /sys/module/mt6789_balance/parameters/.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 comment "CPU frequency scaling drivers"
 
 config CPUFREQ_DT
